meta {
  name: Class results
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/classresults?class={{className}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  class: {{className}}
}

vars:post-response {
  resultsEtag: res.headers.etag
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.className: isDefined
}

docs {
  The endpoint that matters most — the only source of `place`, `timeplus`, `progress`
  and the per-split `place` / `timeplus`, which is why `/export` cannot replace it.

  Differences from legacy `getclassresults`:

  - `splitcontrols` → **`splitControls`**
  - no `hash`, no `status` — use the `ETag`
  - no `DT_RowClass`; each row carries **`changed`** and `startChanged` (UNIX seconds)
  - new per row: `bib`
  - new on the envelope: `isMultiDay`, `isMassStart`, `qualificationLimits`
  - split maps gain a `<code>_changed` key alongside `_status` / `_place` / `_timeplus`

  That last one is a trap: `insertSplitResults` treats any split key not ending in
  `status|timeplus|place` as the *time*, so `_changed` lands in the time bucket. The
  plan strips it in the client.

  `result` and `timeplus` come back as `""` for non-finishers, which the existing
  `parseResultNumber` already handles.

  `start` is present on 100% of rows here, against ~82.5% in `/export`.
}
